[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3494143069","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112224#issuecomment-3494143069","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112224","id":3494143069,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QRGRd","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T00:02:57Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T00:02:57Z","body":"Trying to have `Variant` as this universal middleman is the exact thing we're moving away from, so I have no interest in making a special case for it. This is exposing the unopimized, existing implementation for what it is","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3494143069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3496136310","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112224#issuecomment-3496136310","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112224","id":3496136310,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QYs52","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T09:26:30Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T09:29:41Z","body":"> Trying to have Variant as this universal middleman is the exact thing we're moving away from, so I have no interest in making a special case for it. This is exposing the unopimized, existing implementation for what it is\r\n\r\nI don't think this would qualify for it being a 'universal middleman'. It would be used to confirm whether a `Variant` is a `STRING`, and whether its contents match the literal. I think this is a decent enough use-case; as we can see in this PR it's the most common use case of equality comparisons throughout `Variant`.\r\nThe `operator==` could be declared in `ustring.h`, with the forward declared `Variant`. It would be the same sort of optimization we already have to compare `String` to string literals.\r\n\r\nThe main reason I'm suggesting this at all is that there is no convenient way to make this comparison otherwise. New code would be forced to make new `Variant` from the literal, which is a waste of performance. Or worse, they would use `String(variant) == \"literal\"`, which has different semantics than `variant == Variant(\"literal\")`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3496136310/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3497364950","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112224#issuecomment-3497364950","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112224","id":3497364950,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QdY3W","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T13:51:25Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T13:51:39Z","body":"If different semantics is the main concern, then there's an alternate route that could be taken: unifying comparison semantics. That could remove (or, at least, seriously reduce) the need to eliminate implicit comparison operators. Failing that, it's a reasonable goal to start working towards in general, as inconsistencies across our sorting methods have existed for quite a while now\r\n\r\nWith that in mind, I still disagree with adding any specialized comparisons in this PR. While the concern of different semantics is reasonable, the actual comparisons made by `Variant`/`const char *` are against constrained values that would already be `String` in the first place. Different semantics is only realistically a blocking issue if the types change, but we're consistently passing these `Variant` types as if they're already that expected type; usually a limitation of `TypedArray`/`TypedDictionary` returning contents as `Variant`.\r\n\r\nSomething I *can* do to alleviate concerns is set up some tests that validate this assumption. That is, ensuring every single instance of `(Type(variant) == type) == (variant == Variant(type))` is equivalent. If that isn't sufficent, then we will likely have to bring this up at the next core meeting, as this warrants a much deeper dive on how we should handle comparison operations as a whole.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3497364950/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4871888049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112224#issuecomment-4871888049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112224","id":4871888049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABImMcsQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T01:49:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T01:49:22Z","body":"No longer pursuing this direction; closing","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4871888049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]